# ── Windows stray-device artifacts ────────────────────────────────
# `cmd ... 2>nul` run under a shell with no NUL device (Git Bash, MSYS)
# creates a real 0-byte file called `nul` in the working directory instead
# of discarding the output. It is never wanted, and on Windows it cannot be
# deleted with a plain `rm` once committed.
nul
NUL

